---
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import GuideHeader from "../../components/help/GuideHeader.astro";
import GuideNav from "../../components/help/GuideNav.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/help/Callout.astro";
import Steps from "../../components/help/Steps.astro";
import RelatedGuides from "../../components/help/RelatedGuides.astro";

const sections = [
  { id: "pay", label: "How to pay" },
  { id: "app-only", label: "Pay only in the app" },
  { id: "protected", label: "How you are protected" },
  { id: "scams", label: "Spotting scams" },
  { id: "report", label: "Reporting a problem" },
];
---

<Page
  title="Payments and staying safe"
  description="How payments on NyasaBuy work, how your money is protected until your order arrives, and how to spot and report scams."
>
  <GuideHeader
    title="Payments and staying safe"
    intro="How paying works, how your money is protected, and what to watch out for."
  />
  <GuideNav items={sections} />

  <article class="guide">
    <section id="pay">
      <h2>How to pay</h2>
      <p>
        You can pay with <strong>Airtel Money</strong>,{" "}
        <strong>TNM Mpamba</strong> or a <strong>bank card</strong>. You do not
        need a bank account to shop.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you tap <strong>Pay</strong>, a secure payment page opens. Choose
        how you want to pay and follow the steps. When you are done, you come
        back to NyasaBuy, and a receipt with your payment reference appears in
        your chat with the seller.
      </p>
      <Callout title="Paid but nothing changed?" tone="good">
        <p>
          Give it a minute and refresh your Orders. A payment is confirmed once
          your mobile money provider or bank confirms it. If it still does not
          show, <a href="/#cta">contact us</a> with your payment reference.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </section>

    <section id="app-only">
      <h2>Pay only in the app</h2>
      <Callout title="The one rule that keeps you safe" tone="safety">
        <p>
          <strong>Only payments made in the app are protected.</strong> Never
          send money by Airtel Money, TNM Mpamba, bank transfer or cash in
          advance, even if the seller asks, offers a discount for it, or says
          the app is slow.
        </p>
      </Callout>
      <p>
        If you pay outside the app, NyasaBuy cannot help you get your money
        back if the item never arrives, because we never saw the payment. It
        also means the seller is going around the rules that protect you.
      </p>
      <p>
        If someone asks you to pay outside the app,{" "}
        <strong>do not</strong>. Report them from the <strong>⋯</strong> menu
        in your chat.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="protected">
      <h2>How you are protected</h2>
      <p>When you pay in the app, your money is looked after until you have your order.</p>
      <Steps
        items={[
          {
            title: "You pay",
            body: "The money is taken safely through the app. The seller is told, but does not receive it yet.",
          },
          {
            title: "The seller sends your order",
            body: "They hand it over or deliver it within the time they agreed with you.",
          },
          {
            title: "You confirm you received it",
            body: "Tap Received, and the seller is paid. If you do nothing, the order completes by itself after the confirmation window, so check your orders.",
          },
        ]}
      />
      <p>
        If something is wrong, you can ask for more time or report a problem
        before you confirm. Our team looks at the order and the recent messages,
        and if you were let down, you are refunded.{" "}
        <a href="/help/delivery-and-orders">See what to do if an order is late</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="scams">
      <h2>Spotting scams</h2>
      <p>Take extra care if someone:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Asks you to pay outside the app</strong>, or to move the chat to another app first</li>
        <li><strong>Asks for your PIN, password or card details.</strong> NyasaBuy and its sellers never need them.</li>
        <li><strong>Offers a price that is far too good to be true</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Rushes you</strong> with "pay now or lose it"</li>
        <li><strong>Will not answer simple questions</strong> about the item</li>
      </ul>
      <Callout title="Before you buy" tone="tip">
        <ul>
          <li>Read the description and look at every photo.</li>
          <li>Check the seller's reviews and how long they have been selling.</li>
          <li>For pickup, meet somewhere public and check the item before you confirm.</li>
        </ul>
      </Callout>
    </section>

    <section id="report">
      <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
      <p>There are two kinds of report, and both go to our team.</p>
      <h3>Reporting a chat</h3>
      <p>
        Tap the <strong>⋯</strong> menu in any chat and choose{" "}
        <strong>Report</strong>. Pick the reason, such as:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Asked me to pay outside the app</li>
        <li>Asked for my personal or bank details</li>
        <li>Scam or fraud</li>
        <li>Harassment or abusive messages</li>
        <li>Fake, stolen or prohibited item</li>
        <li>Misleading listing</li>
        <li>Spam, or something else</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Add details in your own words, then send it. Our team reads the recent
        messages and acts. <strong>The other person is not told it was
        you.</strong> You can report a chat at any time, even before you buy
        anything.
      </p>
      <h3>Reporting a problem with an order</h3>
      <p>
        If you have paid and something is wrong, open the order and tap{" "}
        <strong>Report a problem</strong>. Tell us what happened, and we will
        look into it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <RelatedGuides current="payments-and-safety" />
  </article>
</Page>
